  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "When to Hire a General Contractor for Bathroom Renovation",
    "text": "When to Hire a General Contractor for Bathroom Renovation",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Question: Can I handle a bathroom renovation by swapping fixtures myself, or should I hire a general contractor?\n\nAnswer: While simple cosmetic updates like painting a vanity or changing a towel bar are common homeowner tasks, a full bathroom renovation quickly involves complex systems that require professional oversight. \n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n\nHiring a general contractor becomes essential whenever your project touches hidden plumbing, electrical circuits, structural framing, or shower waterproofing. In Colorado municipalities, replacing tub or shower enclosures, altering drain lines, or adding dedicated circuits often requires building permits and inspections. A qualified general contractor coordinates licensed trade specialists, ensures work meets local codes, and manages the project so tasks occur in the right sequence.\n\nFurthermore, bathrooms frequently hide moisture damage behind old tile, around toilet bases, or under subflooring. An experienced contractor knows how to assess damaged floor joists, rebuild framing, and apply complete waterproofing systems like liquid membranes or sheet barriers before setting tile. HH Remodeling LLC provides hands-on project leadership, with owner Abraham Becerra personally overseeing drywall, tile, and finish work while coordinating all trade rough-ins. \n\nIf your renovation involves opening walls, moving plumbing, or replacing shower surrounds, get professional guidance from the start. Call HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your project.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
